<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of rain-affected</p>
<p>four-day English County Championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Saturday:</p>
<p>At Cardiff: Glamorgan v Warwickshire match abandoned.</p>
<p>Warwickshire 151 and 77-3. Glamorgan 551-3 declared. Glamorgan</p>
<p>11 points, Warwickshire 3.</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Nottinghamshire v Worcestershire match</p>
<p>abandoned. Worcestershire 417. Nottinghamshire 196-3. Worcester</p>
<p>8 points, Notts 5.</p>
<p>At Leicester: Leicestershire v Gloucestershire match</p>
<p>abandoned. Gloucestershire 245 and 8-0. Leicestershire 307.</p>
<p>Leicester 10 points Gloucester 8.</p>
<p>At Hove: Sussex v Northamptonshire match abandoned.</p>
<p>Northamptonshire 315 and 41-0. Sussex 411-7 declared. Sussex 11</p>
<p>points Northants 9.</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Lancashire v Durham match abandoned.</p>
<p>Lancashire 506. Durham 201-6. Lancashire 9 points Durham 8.</p>
<p>At The Oval: Surrey v Somerset match abandoned. Somerset</p>
<p>463. Surrey 209-8. Surrey 7 points Somerset 10.</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex v Hampshire match abandoned.  Essex 246</p>
<p>and 442-8 declared. Hampshire 161 and 64-2. Essex 8 points</p>
<p>Hampshire 7.</p>
<p>At Canterbury: Kent 251 and 333. Derbyshire 248 and 248-3</p>
<p>(C.Adams 108, D.Jones 99 not out). Kent and Derbyshire 8 points.</p>
</text>
